<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; Divine Revelation" cic="CCC 50-73, 74-100" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">To use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does the word &laquo;revelation&raquo; mean, and why is it important that God takes the initiative?</li>
<li>Name the three main stages of God's revelation to Israel that the class points out.</li>
<li>Why is Jesus Christ the full and definitive revelation of God, according to the Catechism (CCC 65)?</li>
<li>What are the three channels of transmission of revelation? Explain each one briefly.</li>
<li>What does the Catechism mean when it affirms that &laquo;no new public revelation is to be expected&raquo; (CCC 66)?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>To Reflect and Write</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;right&raquo; answers in these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Have you ever had a &laquo;burning bush&raquo; experience in your life? A moment when you felt God was speaking to you in a special way.</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Describe briefly when it was and what you felt.</p>
<p class="question-block__p" style="margin-top:8px">___________ ___________ ___________ ___________ ___________</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. If God reveals himself gradually, what stage would you say you are living in right now?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Are you in a time of searching, of encounter, of crisis, of deepening?</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Do you find it hard to believe that Jesus is God himself, or does it come naturally to you?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Reflect on which aspects of Jesus' person you find easier or harder to accept as God's revelation.</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. What is your relationship with the Bible? Do you read it as God's Word or do you find it hard to see it that way?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">What would change if you truly believed that God speaks to you through its pages?</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. Do you know someone who, like Saint Paul, had a radical conversion?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Or yourself: have you experienced a deep change in how you see God?</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Prayerful Reading of Exodus 3</h4>
<p>Read Exodus 3:1-15 in your Bible. Then sit in silence for five minutes and imagine you are Moses. What do you see? What do you feel? What does God say to you? Write down what you &laquo;hear&raquo; in your heart.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
